t(37, 925, """From the Mother of the Believers Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stirred in his sleep, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, you did something in your sleep that you did not used to do. He said: "How strange! People of my Ummah will head for the House because of a man of Quraysh who has sought refuge in the House, until, when they are at al-Bayda', they will be swallowed up." We said: O Messenger of Allah, the road brings people together. He said: "Yes, among them are the one who knows what he is doing, the one compelled, and the wayfarer; they perish in one destruction and come forth from different sources; Allah will raise them according to their intentions."» Sahih Muslim""")

h(37, 1550, """To this group among the people of Sham: you will bid farewell to your children, your wives, your fathers and your brothers, then you will never see them again!""")

t(37, 2185, """To travellers in that time and that era, which is not like our time today: do not take the road between Mecca and Medina on that day! Pay attention to a dangerous word in the hadith in Muslim!

((Among them .. the wayfarer)) meaning the traveller ..

The traveller, at the time of the land army's march, will be forced either to join the army of the swallowing or to march with it merely to travel .. then the earth will open and they will all sink into it!

From the Mother of the Believers Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stirred in his sleep, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, you did something in your sleep that you did not used to do. He said: "How strange! People of my Ummah will head for the House because of a man of Quraysh who has sought refuge in the House, until, when they are at al-Bayda', they will be swallowed up." We said: O Messenger of Allah, the road brings people together. He said: "Yes, among them are the one who knows what he is doing, the one compelled, and the wayfarer; they perish in one destruction and come forth from different sources; Allah will raise them according to their intentions."» Sahih Muslim""")

