t(38, 1195, """“And you have returned to where you began, and you have returned to where you began" Sahih Muslim .. The story began at Siffin, and we have been living the story for 1400 years, and the end of the story is in a desert plain (bayda') of the earth, and this is one aspect of "you have returned to where you began"!

As everything began, it ends with the same old attempt .. Siffin will not return .. and the results of Siffin will not be repeated! The coming Siffin is the swallowing! You will enter Siffin in a different way .. you will carry a banner of misguidance and march beneath it, so take what contains salvation for whoever of you wants salvation!

O youth of Sham: some of you will be summoned to a banner of misguidance; if you can flee on that day, then do so, and if you cannot, then march beneath it with the march of one forced, compelled, grieving, bidding farewell to his family, for you will not see them until the Day of Resurrection!

From the Mother of the Believers Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stirred in his sleep, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, you did something in your sleep that you did not used to do. He said: "How strange! People of my Ummah will head for the House because of a man of Quraysh who has sought refuge in the House, until, when they are at al-Bayda', they will be swallowed up." We said: O Messenger of Allah, the road brings people together. He said: "Yes, among them are the one who knows what he is doing, the one compelled, and the wayfarer; they perish in one destruction and come forth from different sources; Allah will raise them according to their intentions."» Sahih Muslim""")

h(38, 2200, """“And you have returned to where you began, and you have returned to where you began." The beginning of the story was Siffin, and the end of the story is a desert plain of the earth. O youth of Sham, listen""")

