t(39, 1420, """The scale of the heart between steadfastness, trembling and severing

A recording today, by the might of Allah the Exalted .. the scale whose steadiness means the firmness of the rope of connection with Allah the Exalted, whose trembling means the trembling of the rope of connection with Allah the Exalted, and whose crashing means the severing of the rope between the servant and his Lord!

This scale exists .. eyes do not see it but understanding grasps it, and the experience of the greatest jihad (the jihad of the self) reveals it .. it is the reason someone asks about a righteous person who went astray: why did he go astray after his righteousness? And about one astray who became righteous: how did he become righteous after being astray?

The picture: the water beneath the heart means the heart being surrounded by trials, a rope connecting the heart and the sky, and in the middle the scale that weighs the movement of what is finer than a hair when it trembles!""")

