t(44, 1240, """Between the Yusuf of 2023 and the Yusuf of 2026

As is my habit, if something concerns me by day or in the evening, I wait for the night prayer, because I "always" read from the Mushaf by opening the Mushaf at random. And as is my habit, I have become used to the Mushaf opening on the right-hand page where I begin the recitation, so that the page and the one facing it answer the question posed in my mind about the matter. Is the same thing always happening over long years a coincidence? The answer is no, because this has happened for long years and always whenever something concerns me and I want an answer to it, not once in a lifetime.

And before that there was the Yusuf of 2023, when one "blind of insight" described me as fabricating dreams and called me a liar. I slept sad, and I saw the real birth of Allah's Prophet Yusuf, peace be upon him, as he was born .. I was in the house of Allah's Prophet Yaqub, peace be upon him, standing in the hall of the house, and to our right was a room in which his wife was giving birth to Yusuf, peace be upon him. Allah's Prophet Yaqub, peace be upon him, stood before me, and one of the elder brothers of Allah's Prophet Yusuf, or a relative, a young man not small, stood to my right, and another man, perhaps a brother or a relative, to my left. It was an old house, somewhat spacious, of very old construction, with woollen rugs covering its floor. Then Yusuf, peace be upon him, was born, and they brought him from the room from his mother, and he was handed to me before everyone. I took him in my arms, placed him close to my chest and looked at him: round-faced, white, his face almost shining from his beauty and the purity and clarity of his good, pure, innocent soul, beautiful with a beauty not seen in any child we have seen in our lives. He looked at me and I looked at him, wrapped in the clothes of a newborn child, a clean white cloth, and he smiled at me. End.

Surat Yusuf is the surah of the true confrontation with the self. It is the great message to mankind to be calm! To get past desires that do not affect their Hereafter! To resist the self's craving .. to know that the decrees of Allah are very specific .. and very exclusive .. and that resisting them is challenging Allah the Exalted in His dominion and on His earth and rejecting His decrees, and that no one will do that except that he destroys himself. Surat Yusuf, where the brothers rejected Allah's decree concerning Yusuf and decided that they would draw his destiny for him, and thought they had drawn it for him when they planned for him to become a slave sold in the slave markets by putting him in a well! Then he became the second man in a great kingdom!

Elevation on earth is a decision from Allah the Exalted alone, and is not sought by mere human desire .. so Surat Yusuf is a message to all people .. be calm .. submit to Allah ... surrender to Allah .. or else it is certain disgrace, because the Lord does not accept anyone saying to Him: Why?!

Surat Yusuf is a command from our Mighty Lord that we meet Him on the Day of Resurrection without having posed in our lives the question of the first disbelief: Why him? Why him and not me? The question of the first disbelief! The question Iblis said. So where is he today? In a lofty station, or in the lowest of the low?""")

h(45, 400, """The punishment of injustice is the blotting out of insight! In 2023, the story of an oppressor and the story of an oppressed man who saw the real birth of Allah's Prophet Yusuf!""")

t(45, 1015, """Except Jerusalem, it is the only exception .. two kingdoms ruling the world from Jerusalem: a Solomonic one that has passed, and the other that has not yet come!

So where is the return of the other kingdoms of history that arose from various lands and preoccupied the world?! Muslim and non-Muslim! None of them has returned!
The Romans, the English and the French, and among the virtuous kingdoms the first caliphate, then the biting kingship, up to the Ottoman!

The matter of their not returning is not that they were all wrong. Allah the Almighty forbid, for among them is the first caliphate from the pure city of Medina. Rather it is the way of Allah the Almighty in kingdoms and great states, a way of which we understand some and are ignorant of some, and to Allah our Mighty Lord belongs the conclusive wisdom, holy are His names and attributes, magnified in the heavens and on earth, exalted greatly, All-Glorious, All-Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit.

Medina .. Kufa .. Damascus .. Baghdad .. Cairo.. Istanbul

Cities from which the whole Islamic world, or important parts of it, was ruled

Cairo: Fatimids and Mamluks
Kufa: the whole old Islamic world except Sham

The capitals of the Islamic states passed away, and those capitals never returned again!""")

